{"name":"Musk Deer","hex":"#7e5b58","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"musk deer","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hoofed mammal of the genus Moschus, inhabiting East Asia, the Himalayas, and Siberia. The males secrete musk and possess tusks."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/musk_deer"}],"entries":[{"title":"Musk deer","blocks":[{"text":"Musk deer can refer to any one, or all seven, of the species that make up Moschus, the only extant genus of the family Moschidae. Despite being commonly called deer, they are not true deer belonging to the family Cervidae, but rather their family is closely related to Bovidae, the group that contains antelopes, bovines, sheep, and goats. The musk deer family differs from cervids, or true deer, by lacking antlers and preorbital glands also, possessing only a single pair of teats, a gallbladder, a caudal gland, a pair of canine tusks and—of particular economic importance to humans—a musk gland."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Musk_deer_in_Edinburgh_Zoo.jpg/330px-Musk_deer_in_Edinburgh_Zoo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Musk_deer","wikidata":"Q3866060"},{"title":"Musk","blocks":[{"text":"Musk is a class of aromatic substances commonly used as base notes in perfumery. They include glandular secretions from animals such as the musk deer, numerous plants emitting similar fragrances, and artificial substances with similar odors. Musk was a name originally given to a substance with a strong odor obtained from a gland of the musk deer. The substance has been used as a popular perfume fixative since ancient times and is one of the most expensive animal products in the world. The name originates from the Late Greek μόσχος 'moskhos', from Persian mushk, in turn from Sanskrit मुष्क muṣka derived from Proto-Indo-European noun múh₂s meaning \"mouse\". The deer gland was thought to resemble a scrotum. The term is applied to various plants and animals of similar smell and has come to encompass a wide variety of aromatic substances with similar odors, despite their often differing chemical structures and molecular shapes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Naturalists_Library_-_Mammalia_-_Volume_III_-_The_Thibetian_Musk.jpg/330px-Naturalists_Library_-_Mammalia_-_Volume_III_-_The_Thibetian_Musk.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Musk","wikidata":"Q323461"},{"title":"Deer","blocks":[{"text":"A deer or true deer is a hoofed ruminant ungulate of the family Cervidae. Cervidae is divided into subfamilies Cervinae and Capreolinae. Male deer of almost all species, as well as female reindeer, grow and shed new antlers each year. These antlers are bony extensions of the skull and are often used for combat between males."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Family_Cervidae_five_species.jpg/330px-Family_Cervidae_five_species.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deer","wikidata":"Q23390"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Moschidae_distribution.png/500px-Moschidae_distribution.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Moschidae_distribution.png/500px-Moschidae_distribution.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMoschidae_distribution.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Porte_musc_global.jpg/500px-Porte_musc_global.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Porte_musc_global.jpg/1280px-Porte_musc_global.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Porte_musc_global.jpg/500px-Porte_musc_global.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Skull of a buck showing the characteristic teeth","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APorte_musc_global.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Zwerghirsch-Micromeryx-Skelett.jpg/500px-Zwerghirsch-Micromeryx-Skelett.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Zwerghirsch-Micromeryx-Skelett.jpg/1280px-Zwerghirsch-Micromeryx-Skelett.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/Zwerghirsch-Micromeryx-Skelett.jpg/500px-Zwerghirsch-Micromeryx-Skelett.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Skeleton of Micromeryx showing the general skeletal features","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AZwerghirsch-Micromeryx-Skelett.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Moschus_berezovskii_-_Kunming_Natural_History_Museum_of_Zoology_-_DSC02453.JPG/120px-Moschus_berezovskii_-_Kunming_Natural_History_Museum_of_Zoology_-_DSC02453.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Moschus_berezovskii_-_Kunming_Natural_History_Museum_of_Zoology_-_DSC02453.JPG/250px-Moschus_berezovskii_-_Kunming_Natural_History_Museum_of_Zoology_-_DSC02453.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Moschus_berezovskii_-_Kunming_Natural_History_Museum_of_Zoology_-_DSC02453.JPG/120px-Moschus_berezovskii_-_Kunming_Natural_History_Museum_of_Zoo